      "field_name": "diagnostic_criteria",
      "value": "clinical features (stiffness, rigidity, spasms, lordosis), EMG findings (continuous motor activity abolished by diazepam), anti-GAD65 autoantibodies",
      "quote": "the following criteria: (1) initial stiffness and rigidity in the axial muscles; (2) slow progression of stiffness to include proximal limb muscles ... (3) a fixed deformity of the spine, as in lordosis ... (4) the presence of superimposed episodic spasms precipitated by sudden movements, jarring noise, and emotional upset; (5) normal findings on motor and sensory nerve examinations; (6) normal intellect; and (7) electromyographic findings typical of continuous motor activity that can be abolished by intravenous or orally administered diazepam. Antiglutamic acid decarboxylase (antiGAD65) autoantibodies disrupt the function of gamma-aminobutyric acid (GABA)",
      "confidence": "high"
